WHATNOW

What tam-clam is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-24, with W20 (0.3.0)


STATE

  Version 0.3.0, Phase P4 in progress (indexed and associative arrays),
  on branch dev. 0.3.0 adds:
  - sparse indexed arrays and hashed associative arrays in
    include/tam-clam/array.h, src/array.c, and src/var.c (never exported
    to envp, readonly-protected, scalar-to-array conversion);
  - bash array syntax in src/lex.c, src/parse.c, src/func.c, src/lint.c,
    src/exec.c: a=(...), a+=(...), a[sub]=v, a[sub]+=v, scalar +=, and
    compound args to declare/typeset/readonly/export;
  - parameter expansions in src/expand.c: ${a[sub]}, ${a[@]}, ${a[*]},
    ${#a[@]}, ${#a[sub]}, ${!a[@]}, ${!a[*]}, POSIX ops on elements, and
    element-wise pattern trimming (${a[@]#pat}, ${a[@]%pat});
  - arithmetic indexing in src/arith.c ($((a[i])), a[i]+=1, ++a[i]);
  - declare/typeset (-a/-A/-p/-r/-x/-g/+x) in src/bi_declare.c, unset
    'a[sub]' and array printing in src/builtins_special.c, and read -a
    in src/builtins_io.c;
  - tests/test_array.c (123 checks), tests/spec/arrays.test.sh (22 cases
    against bash --posix), fuzz seeds, and sandbox/demo-0.3.0-arrays.
  readelf -d lists only libc.so.6. make test, make sanitize, and make
  fuzz pass.

  Fred's decisions so far are in ROADMAP.md and the plans: POSIX.1-2024
  is the target; the Tamlinux-wide keybinding standard lives in
  tamlinux/arch/keybindings.md and tam-clam implements it in
  arch/keys.md (no vi mode, no built-in readline map, VINTR=Ctrl+\,
  VSUSP=Ctrl+P, Ctrl+F history search, Ctrl+Q quit); FUNCNEST sets the
  function recursion limit; signed 64-bit arithmetic overflow is a
  reported error; echo recognizes -n only and does not interpret
  backslash escapes by default.


